{"availability":"available","full":"nirmala-sharma/doculens","name":"doculens","description":"Citation-first RAG assistant that answers developer questions from trusted documentation with source citations, evidence passages, and hallucination guardrails.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-12T16:49:10Z","updated":"2026-10-03T21:44:06Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://brilliant-beijinho-a6069f.netlify.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T21:35:08.054Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T21:35:08.054Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T21:35:08.054Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:46.161Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-04T21:35:08.054Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Upload any PDF and ask questions about it. Get answers with source citations, not hallucinations.","DocuLens is a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system that lets you chat with your own PDF documents — resumes, reports, documentation, research papers — and get answers backed by exact source citations.","You upload a PDF. You ask: \"What projects did this person work on?\" DocuLens embeds your question, retrieves the most relevant chunks from your document, passes them to an LLM, and returns a grounded answer with the source file cited."],"features":["PDF upload — drag in any PDF and start asking questions immediately","Source filtering — answers are pulled only from your uploaded document, not mixed with other data","Deduplication — re-uploading the same file replaces old chunks, no duplicates","Similarity guardrail — refuses to answer when no relevant content is found","Chat-style UI — clean dark interface with typing indicators and inline source citations"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nirmala-sharma/doculens/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"87e8ab766836033c8fba3603bf30f0d5f05ac14ead13b6ca3d229c1c104585a9","extractedAt":"2